From: SteamAC contributors
Subject: [PATCH] snd: fix microphone callback format and pace capture startup

Initialize Float32 capture callback stride/channels before AudioOutputUnitStart.
Do not complete capture buffers queued during PREPARE; ALSA has not started its
hardware clock yet. While waiting for the microphone or permission, pace silence
at the negotiated sample rate instead of completing all queued buffers at once.
The latter moved the guest hardware pointer ahead of time, causing continuous
XRUN/STOP/START loops which also cancelled the asynchronous microphone worker.

Include a regression test for PREPARE and startup-silence timing.

--- a/src/devices/src/virtio/snd/audio_backends/coreaudio.rs
+++ b/src/devices/src/virtio/snd/audio_backends/coreaudio.rs
@@ -1668,6 +1668,10 @@
                 staging: Vec::new(),
             },
         };
+        // The callback renders device Float32, not the guest's S16 format. Publish its
+        // stride and channel count before CoreAudio can call it (also on mono/stereo switches).
+        shared.frame_bytes.store(dev_fmt.mBytesPerFrame, Ordering::Relaxed);
+        shared.channels.store(dev_fmt.mChannelsPerFrame, Ordering::Relaxed);
         // The input callback needs the unit pointer before the unit starts producing; it reads
         // it lock-free from `shared.unit`.
         shared.unit.store(state.unit.au, Ordering::Release);
@@ -1982,6 +1986,7 @@
